{
 "id": "bigville_build_construct",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R12 (block 260000) -- CONSTRUCTION economy. A BUILDER consumes RAW MATERIALS (timber+stone) + LABOUR (a per-tick step whose SPEED = the builder's CONSTRUCTION skill level) over TIME (multi-tick, tick_armed) to raise a durable BUILDING on an OWNED, FUNDED plot (R13 precondition, bb_consume/bb_raise); building on ANOTHER'S land is refused = TRESPASS (bb_trespass; unowned land matches neither -> refused as absence). Funding is PERSONAL (coin, bb_fund) or a BANK LOAN (bb_loan: R7 reserves -> builder coin + a BuildLoan that ACCRUES like a mortgage, bb_loan_accrue = IDiv(balance*(10000+rate_bp),10000), integer coin). An existing building is MODIFIED / ADDED-ON (bb_addon: more materials -> size+capacity grow). bb_raise ALSO marks the plot's map cell blocked+occludes (the map mutation; the mutable-world seed severs the adjacency). Composes existing DSL Terms only; ZERO new Rust.",
